1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:19,201
Cassius wore his father's jacket to the rescue. It was too loose
through the shoulders and a little short at the wrists. He had found
it in the shed with the Red Saint, folded in a box beside old race
programs. The leather smelled faintly of oil and the kind of time
nobody can buy back.

2
00:00:19,451 --> 00:00:43,578
I saw him standing beside the helicopter and didn't make a joke. Tank
did. Nigga, you dressed like you about to apologize to a motorcycle.
Cassius looked down at himself. It's my father's. Tank's face changed.
Then it's a good jacket. Cassius nodded. Yeah. That was the whole
conversation. Sometimes my brother knew exactly when to stop being
funny.

3
00:00:43,828 --> 00:01:08,396
The Sovereign Sun had moved overnight to a private anchorage beyond
Isla Gloria's northern cliffs. Its public crew were ashore. Captain
Morcant commanded the men left aboard, along with the two prisoners
the duke had kept out of sight for seven years. Odette had received
word from a crewman who had managed to leave with the opera workers.
Morcant planned to sail before sunset.

4
00:01:08,646 --> 00:01:34,835
Nobody knew where. We weren't letting the afternoon decide for us. Our
pilot was a woman named Selene Price, thirty-nine, former rescue
flyer, hired by Rocco after Porsche explained that his casino would
benefit from being remembered fondly by the people currently saving
his guests. Selene looked at the list of passengers, then at Bruno.
You're two, she told him. He looked at Tank.

5
00:01:35,085 --> 00:02:01,246
So is he. Nigga, Tank said, I don't split fares. Selene pointed at
Tank, then Bruno. "Separate aircraft." "Nigga, she divided us," Tank
said. "She weighed us," Bruno answered. "Emotionally?" "Nigga,
structurally." I stepped between them. "Both niggas get there. Neither
nigga takes the roof off the helicopter. That's the agreement." Selene
looked at me. "You are the one I'm worried about." Shawna nodded.

6
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:27,859
"She picked the correct nigga immediately." "Y'all trust me or not?" I
asked. "Nigga, I trust the result," Tank said. "Transportation be
having a difficult middle." We took two helicopters. Shawna came in
mine with Cassius and Inez. Tank, Bruno and two of Odette's officers
took the second. Rosa stayed on the rescue yacht below with Mercedes,
Porsche, Lark, Mateo and a medical crew.

7
00:02:28,109 --> 00:02:51,354
Esteban waited there too, holding the goat trophy in both hands like
Nero might recognize it before he recognized the years on his friend's
face. Before we boarded, Shawna caught my wrist. You're quiet.
Thinking. About? The promise. She looked toward Cassius. Then back at
me. You promised to go. You're going. Bring your eyes with you. I
kissed her.

8
00:02:51,604 --> 00:03:15,642
Nigga, you keep making good points at inconvenient times. That is
marriage. We lifted off. The island passed beneath us, bright roofs
and green hills. Then the northern cliffs opened to the sea, and the
Sovereign Sun appeared in the cove below, white decks empty, gold trim
shining like the ship hadn't done a damn thing wrong. Two armed boats
circled it.

9
00:03:15,892 --> 00:03:40,594
Morcant had expected trouble. Nigga, he had underestimated the
transportation. Selene brought us low over the water. The first guard
boat turned toward us. A gun flashed from its bow. The helicopter
jolted as a shot struck something behind the cabin, loud enough to
make Cassius flinch and Inez reach for his good hand. Selene didn't
even swear. Rude, she said.

10
00:03:40,844 --> 00:04:01,923
Then she took us over the yacht's stern. The second helicopter came
across from the other side. Tank stood at its open door, one hand
locked on the frame, shouting down at the men on deck like he had come
to collect a personal debt from the entire boat. Police, niggas! I
shook my head. Nigga love my job.

11
00:04:02,173 --> 00:04:23,887
Selene set us onto the upper platform hard enough to bounce. I was out
before the rotor slowed, Shawna behind me, Cassius and Inez moving
toward the stairwell together. The guards on the deck had turned
toward Tank's helicopter. By the time they saw us, I had already
reached the first one. He swung his rifle toward me.

12
00:04:24,137 --> 00:04:42,938
I hit him with my shoulder and drove him into a sun lounger. The
weapon skidded away. Shawna covered the second guard until Odette's
officer took him down. The third ran toward the bridge. I followed.
The yacht shook under our feet as its engines woke. Morcant was
leaving.

13
00:04:43,188 --> 00:04:59,992
Nigga had seen two helicopters land on his boat and decided the
solution was a different patch of ocean. I reached the bridge door
just as he came out. Morcant was forty-six, heavy through the chest,
shaved head, white shirt open at the throat.

14
00:05:00,242 --> 00:05:23,722
He carried a pistol in one hand and a ceremonial saber in the other,
because apparently he couldn't decide whether to be a captain or a
warning label. You're on my ship, he said. Nigga, your captain
downstairs. His jaw tightened. Celadon lost his ship. No. A nigga
stole it. He lifted the pistol. I moved behind the door as the shot
struck the frame.

15
00:05:23,972 --> 00:05:42,678
The wood splintered against my shoulder. I hit him before he could
bring the gun back around, and we went through the bridge doorway
together, knocking a chair across the floor. He was strong. Fast too.
He drove an elbow into my ribs, caught my jacket and threw me against
the console.

16
00:05:42,928 --> 00:06:05,960
Pain flashed through my side, old and familiar enough to make me angry
before I was afraid. Nigga, I said, you picked the sentimental side.
He swung the saber. The blade cut through my sleeve and bit into the
chair behind me. I grabbed his wrist, struck him hard and sent the
pistol out of his other hand. It slid beneath the console.

17
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:27,940
He tried to pull the saber free. I took the chair with it. For one
ridiculous second we stood holding opposite ends of a chair with a
sword through it. Morcant stared at me. I stared back. Nigga, this is
embarrassing for your profession. Then I drove the chair into him. He
fell against the bridge window. The glass cracked.

18
00:06:28,190 --> 00:06:49,381
He came back swinging, no longer interested in dignity, and struck me
across the mouth. I tasted blood. Hit him twice. He staggered, caught
the edge of the console and reached for a hidden knife. Shawna
appeared in the doorway. Don't. Her gun was steady. He looked at her.
At me. At the knife halfway out of his sleeve.

19
00:06:49,631 --> 00:07:11,686
For one moment he had a chance to be smart. He chose differently. He
lunged toward her. I caught him around the waist and drove both of us
through the side door onto the narrow exterior walk. We struck the
rail. It bent. Morcant's knife flashed past my face and went into the
water below. He grabbed my collar. The rail gave.

20
00:07:11,936 --> 00:07:32,878
We went over together. I caught the lower edge with one hand. Morcant
caught my sleeve. Below us, the yacht's wake boiled white against the
hull. Nigga, I gasped, you heavy for a man with no future. He tried to
climb me. The sleeve tore. I reached down with my free hand, caught
his wrist and held him for a second.

21
00:07:33,128 --> 00:07:52,217
I wasn't doing it because he deserved a beautiful ending. I wanted him
alive to say what he knew, and I didn't want Cassius's reunion to
begin with my body in the water. Morcant looked up at me. Then he
pulled the small gun from his belt with his free hand. Nigga had
learned nothing.

22
00:07:52,467 --> 00:08:11,081
I let go of his wrist and hauled myself toward the rail as the shot
went wide. Morcant fell. The sea took him out of sight. I hung there
for one hard breath. Then Bruno's hand closed around my forearm.
Nigga, he said, you weigh less than the table. He lifted me onto the
deck.

23
00:08:11,331 --> 00:08:32,503
I rolled onto my back, coughing, while Shawna knelt beside me and put
both hands on my face. You here? Yeah. Stay here. Trying. She kissed
my bloody mouth without caring what it did to her lipstick. Behind
her, Tank came onto the bridge carrying a man by the back of his
shirt. This nigga knows the cabins.

24
00:08:32,753 --> 00:08:57,015
The man nodded so fast I worried about his neck. I know. I know. I
stood. My knees complained. Nothing blue. Nothing borrowed. Just my
own body reminding me it had participated in the morning. Show us, I
said. We went down through the ship. The corridor below the bridge
smelled of polish, old air and food carried past doors without
stopping.

25
00:08:57,265 --> 00:09:19,942
At the far end stood two locked cabins. The guard's hands shook as he
opened the first. Captain Celadon sat beside the window. He was fifty-
nine, beard gone white, shoulders narrow beneath a clean shirt. He
looked up at us without surprise at first, as if he had practiced
disappointment often enough to make hope wait outside.

26
00:09:20,192 --> 00:09:45,494
Then he saw the little white bird in Cassius's hand. Nero? he
whispered. His son, Cassius said. Celadon stood. Slowly. One hand on
the chair. My God, he said. You came. Cassius was already at the
second door. The guard opened it. Nero Chrome stood on the other side.
Fifty-four. Gray in his hair. Leaner than the photographs. One cheek
marked by an old scar.

27
00:09:45,744 --> 00:10:05,086
He wore a plain blue shirt with the sleeves rolled up and held a book
open in one hand, thumb keeping his place as if some part of him had
refused to believe any interruption could be final. He looked at
Cassius. The book fell. Nobody spoke. Cassius took one step. Nero took
one.

28
00:10:05,336 --> 00:10:23,790
Then they were holding each other, the father's arms around the son's
shoulders, the son's face pressed into the blue shirt, both of them
making sounds no proud man would choose in front of strangers and
neither caring that we were there. I stood in the doorway. Shawna's
hand found mine.

29
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:48,571
Nigga, I had won four keys, three kinds of race and a gold belt off
the strongest man in a yacht club. None of it made my chest feel like
watching Cassius become somebody's child again without becoming
smaller. Nero held his son's face between both hands. Look at you.
Cassius laughed through tears. Look at me? Nigga, look at you. Nero
laughed too.

30
00:10:48,821 --> 00:11:05,858
Then his eyes moved over the jacket. You kept it. Kept everything.
Inez stood behind Cassius with one hand over her mouth. Nero saw her.
Amalia's girl. She nodded. He held out an arm, and she went into it
with Cassius still beside him.

31
00:11:06,108 --> 00:11:28,598
For a moment the old race had three people in the same room who had
all been waiting to finish the same sentence. Celadon touched my
badge. Captain? Aiden. He looked toward the ceiling, listening to the
engines. Who's steering my ship? I looked at Tank. Tank looked at
Bruno. Bruno looked back at me. Celadon closed his eyes. Move.

32
00:11:28,848 --> 00:11:44,944
Nigga walked past all of us like seven years had been an inconvenient
delay between him and his bridge. We followed him up. The remaining
guards had surrendered to Odette's officers. Morcant's boats had been
intercepted outside the cove.

33
00:11:45,194 --> 00:12:10,355
On the bridge, Celadon took the wheel, looked over the controls,
touched one familiar brass fitting with two fingers and brought the
Sovereign Sun around toward the harbor. Nero stood beside him. Cassius
stood beside Nero. The ship finally looked like it knew where it was
going. Our rescue yacht came alongside near the mainland quay. Esteban
waited at the rail holding the goat trophy.

34
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:31,812
Nero saw it from the bridge. He stopped breathing for a second. Then
he laughed. A huge, broken laugh that brought his son turning toward
him in alarm. That ugly fucking goat. Esteban lifted it higher. I kept
second place, he called. Nero came down the gangway slowly. Esteban
met him halfway.

35
00:12:32,062 --> 00:12:55,400
For a moment they stood facing each other, seven years between them
and a little silver animal held like a peace offering neither man knew
how to name. I believed them, Esteban said. Nero's face changed. I
know. I should have believed you. Yes. Esteban bowed his head. Nero
took the trophy from him. Then he put his other hand on his friend's
shoulder.

36
00:12:55,650 --> 00:13:14,042
Tell me about her, he said. Esteban looked up. Amalia? All the things
we remember before that day. They sat together on the deck. Cassius
stayed near them. Inez sat beside him. Nobody hurried the stories.
Captain Celadon's wife arrived at the harbor an hour later.

37
00:13:14,292 --> 00:13:35,880
Renee, fifty-seven, dark curls threaded with gray, carrying no bag,
wearing the first shoes she had found when Odette called. She ran the
length of the quay. Celadon met her at the gangway and held her like
the ship beneath his feet had become irrelevant. The harbor cheered.
Not just for me this time. For the men coming home.

38
00:13:36,130 --> 00:13:59,298
I stood with Shawna at the rail while the sun moved west. She touched
the split in my lip. You promised to go. Yeah. You brought them back.
Yeah. She smiled, eyes bright. Damn, boy. I looked down at the cross.
Magnificent, I said. Nigga, Tank called from behind us, y'all flirting
in the middle of a national event. I pulled Shawna closer.

39
00:13:59,548 --> 00:14:01,767
Then the nation can learn something.
